 ## Logging
 
+## Controlled Git tools
+
+DevSpace always exposes `git_status`, `git_fetch`, `git_pull`, `git_switch`,
+`git_stage`, `git_commit`, and `git_push`. These tools run Git through fixed
+argument arrays rather than the shell and operate only when the opened workspace
+root is exactly the repository root after canonical-path resolution.
+
+`git_pull` always uses `--ff-only`. Pull and branch-switch operations refuse a
+dirty working tree and return the modified paths; they never stash, reset, or
+discard changes. `git_stage` requires explicit workspace-relative paths.
+Destructive reset and clean operations are intentionally not exposed.
+
+Direct commits and pushes to `main` are denied by default. Configure additional
+protected branches in `~/.devspace/config.json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "git": {
+    "protectedBranches": ["main", "release"]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+For exceptional administrator-controlled workflows only, set
+`DEVSPACE_GIT_ALLOW_COMMIT_TO_PROTECTED_BRANCHES=1` and/or
+`DEVSPACE_GIT_ALLOW_PUSH_TO_PROTECTED_BRANCHES=1` in the service environment.
+Those switches should not be used for normal agent development.
